    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d504">

                <pb facs="0964" n="942" sameAs="frus:frus1950v05/pg942"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">486.118/6–2850</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of Defense</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-06-28">28 June 1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: As you suggested in your
                    letter of 25 May 1950, I have reviewed the situation regarding arms exports to
                    Israel and the Arab states. I am in agreement with you that broad policy
                    considerations may warrant the approval of limited amounts <pb facs="0965"
                        n="943" xml:id="pg943"/> of material to these states at intervals over a
                    period of time. Accordingly, I will be glad to acquiesce in your approval of the
                    export to Israel and the Arab states of such materials as AT–6 aircraft, machine guns and ammunition, radar equipment, half
                    tracks and other material of a similar military potential where you determine
                    that broad policy considerations override the strictly military views previously
                    furnished you in regard to exports to these states.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Louis Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
